ft proof of concept sourc id src note 08 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2026 02 27 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3974113940 author pellar creat 2026 02 27t17 20 46z updat 2026 02 27t17 21 05z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 11 27 action item nico hertz open an issu describ the runtim profil problem and propos mode semant trade off creat a smaller pr to allow disabl runtim tracer integr explor flaki test issu in contrib maintain provid onboard support buddi help via slack for new contributor\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8738b66a8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3974113940.md\", \"id\": \"9b5b6f01e95cbce3\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.5939947103701922, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.5000000005288462, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8133157, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3974113940.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8738b66a8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3974113940.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3974113940.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 3929, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:30\", \"token_count\": 1330, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-08]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2026-02-27\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3974113940  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2026-02-27T17:20:46Z · **Updated**: 2026-02-27T17:21:05Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-11-27  \\n\\n## Attendees\\n\\n- Robert Pająk  \\n\\n- Damien Mathieu  \\n\\n- Nico Hertz  \\n\\n- Michal Jarmolkiewicz  \\n\\n- Bryan Boreham  \\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-08]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2026-02-27\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3974113940  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2026-02-27T17:20:46Z · **Updated**: 2026-02-27T17:21:05Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-11-27  \\n\\n## Discussions\\n\\n### 1. PR Review Request (Profiling / Runtime Tracer)\\n\\n- Request for reviews on Nico’s PR related to Go runtime profiling (`pprof`) integration.\\n\\n- Current behavior: each span creates a runtime tracing **task**, which introduces noise in profiles.\\n\\n- Proposal:\\n\\n  - Provide more control over task/region creation.\\n\\n  - Different modes:\\n\\n    - **Default**: create a task only for the root span.\\n\\n    - **Auto mode**: task for root span, regions for child spans.\\n\\n    - **Manual mode**: explicit task/region instrumentation by the user.\\n\\n  - Optional async-style hint to indicate spans that cross goroutines.\\n\\n- Key considerations:\\n\\n  - Tasks can span multiple goroutines; regions must stay within a single goroutine.\\n\\n  - Changing public tracing APIs is sensitive and tightly coupled to the specification.\\n\\n  - Risk of breaking changes for existing instrumentation (e.g., Kafka libraries).\\n\\n- Recommendation:\\n\\n  - Start with a smaller, incremental change (e.g., ability to disable runtime tracing integration).\\n\\n  - Open an issue describing:\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src note 08 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2026 02 27 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3974113940 author pellar creat 2026 02 27t17 20 46z updat 2026 02 27t17 21 05z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 11 27 attende robert paj ą k damien mathieu nico hertz michal jarmolkiewicz bryan boreham sourc id src note 08 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2026 02 27 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3974113940 author pellar creat 2026 02 27t17 20 46z updat 2026 02 27t17 21 05z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 11 27 discuss 1 pr review request profil runtim tracer request for review on nico s pr relat to go runtim profil pprof integr current behavior each span creat a runtim trace task which introduc nois in profil propos provid more control over task region creation differ mode default creat a task onli for the root span auto mode task for root span region for child span manual mode explicit task region instrument by the user option async style hint to indic span that cross goroutin key consider task can span multipl goroutin region must stay within a singl goroutin chang public trace api is sensit and tight coupl to the specif risk of break chang for exist instrument e g kafka librari recommend start with a smaller increment chang e g abil to disabl runtim trace integr open an issu describ\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8738b66a8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3974113940.md\", \"id\": \"5e119fac2b91a374\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.5348218765809911, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.4230769236871302, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7955601, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3974113940.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8738b66a8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3974113940.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3974113940.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 3929, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:30\", \"token_count\": 1330, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"- Two non-observability items noted:\\n\\n  - Sync map / atomics for fixed bucket histograms.\\n\\n  - Exemplar reservoir changes.\\n\\n- Safe to slip to next release; include if ready.\\n\\n### 4. Stabilizing new attribute value types\\n\\n- Discussion about stabilizing new spec attribute types (byte arrays, “any” type).\\n\\n- Prototype implementation exists and needs review.\\n\\n- Considered tricky; careful review needed around limits and types.\\n\\n### 5. Processor `Enabled` method\\n\\n- Proposal from Robert to move `Enabled` from filter processor to main processor interface.\\n\\n- Spec now stabilized and allows this.\\n\\n- Pros: consistent API, less ad-hoc type assertion/boilerplate in docs.\\n\\n- Con: processors that are “always enabled” need a trivial `Enabled() bool { return true }`.\\n\\n- General agreement; will revisit for final confirmation.\\n\\n### 6. OTLP `insecure` support (logs, env vars, spec)\\n\\n- PR adds `insecure` (env var) support for OTLP **logs**, matching traces/metrics.\\n\\n- HTTP OTLP config historically messy; env vars common in practice.\\n\\n- Spec unclear due to moratorium on env vars.\\n\\n- Direction: add logs support in Go; push for spec clarity later.\\n\\n### 7. Collector protobuf changes & PDataGen\\n\\n- Collector removed dependency on Go protobuf types; now uses `pdataGen`.\\n\\n- Large internal rewrite; significant line count reduction.\\n\\n- Benchmarks improved (fewer allocations).\\n\\n- Some cross-language quirks surfaced but manageable.\\n\\n- Go SIG interested in exploring similar approaches; needs more benchmarking.\\n\\n### 8. KubeCon & talks\\n\\n- First SIG meeting since KubeCon.\\n\\n- Members encouraged to share notable talks and videos once available.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-07]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-26\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3581463689  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-26T14:02:28Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-26T16:36:01Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-11-20  \\n\\n## Decisions\\n\\n- Merge OTelConf RC support PR as-is (pending normal review).\\n\\n- Track experimental API structure review (e.g., `x` submodule) under the `1.40.0` milestone.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"two non observ item note sync map atom for fix bucket histogram exemplar reservoir chang safe to slip to next releas includ if readi 4 stabil new attribut valu type discuss about stabil new spec attribut type byte array ani type prototyp implement exist and need review consid tricki care review need around limit and type 5 processor enabl method propos from robert to move enabl from filter processor to main processor interfac spec now stabil and allow this pro consist api less ad hoc type assert boilerpl in doc con processor that are alway enabl need a trivial enabl bool return true general agreement will revisit for final confirm 6 otlp insecur support log env var spec pr add insecur env var support for otlp log match trace metric http otlp config histor messi env var common in practic spec unclear due to moratorium on env var direct add log support in go push for spec clariti later 7 collector protobuf chang pdatagen collector remov depend on go protobuf type now us pdatagen larg intern rewrit signific line count reduct benchmark improv fewer alloc some cross languag quirk surfac but manag go sig interest in explor similar approach need more benchmark 8 kubecon talk first sig meet sinc kubecon member encourag to share notabl talk and video onc avail sourc id src note 07 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 26 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3581463689 author pellar creat 2025 11 26t14 02 28z updat 2025 11 26t16 36 01z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 11 20 decis merg otelconf rc support pr ais pend normal review track experiment api structur review e g x submodul under the 140 0 mileston\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"874202ba8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3581463689.md\", \"id\": \"2174523acdce943d\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3570992942133876, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.19230769316198223, \"vector_similarity\": 0.74161303, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3581463689.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874202ba8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3581463689.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3581463689.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 3959, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:22\", \"token_count\": 1379, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-07]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-26\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3581463689  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-26T14:02:28Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-26T16:36:01Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-11-20  \\n\\n## Attendees\\n\\n- Tyler Yahn  \\n\\n- Owen Williams  \\n\\n- Sam Xie\\n\\n- Alex Boten  \\n\\n- David Ashpole  \\n\\n- Bryan Boreham  \\n\\n- (Mentioned: Robert Pająk)\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-07]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-26\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3581463689  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-26T14:02:28Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-26T16:36:01Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-11-20  \\n\\n## Discussions\\n\\n### 1. Next Go release & OTelConf RC support\\n\\n- Release blocked on RC support module; PR needs reviews.\\n\\n- Requested changes from Alex do not need to be in the current PR.\\n\\n- Module is `0.x`; breaking changes acceptable later.\\n\\n- Avoid exposing public API known to be removed immediately.\\n\\n- Discussed handling experimental features:\\n\\n  - `WithExperimentalFeatures`-style flag likely unhelpful.\\n\\n  - Possible `x` submodule to clearly isolate experimental APIs.\\n\\n  - Aligns with OTel-wide push for opt-in experimental features.\\n\\n### 2. HTTP default client deprecation (OTel HTTP)\\n\\n- Work deprecating default HTTP client usage is in progress.\\n\\n- `POST`/`GET` helpers rely on `http.DefaultClient` and limit configurability.\\n\\n- Follow-up PRs exist; need review for inclusion in upcoming release.\\n\\n### 3. Observability work & non-blocking PRs\\n\\n- Several observability PRs (e.g., self-observability for OTel gRPC) are ongoing, not release-blocking.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src note 07 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 26 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3581463689 author pellar creat 2025 11 26t14 02 28z updat 2025 11 26t16 36 01z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 11 20 attende tyler yahn owen william sam xie alex boten david ashpol bryan boreham mention robert paj ą k sourc id src note 07 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 26 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3581463689 author pellar creat 2025 11 26t14 02 28z updat 2025 11 26t16 36 01z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 11 20 discuss 1 next go releas otelconf rc support releas block on rc support modul pr need review request chang from alex do not need to be in the current pr modul is 0 x break chang accept later avoid expos public api known to be remov immedi discuss handl experiment featur withexperimentalfeatur style flag like unhelp possibl x submodul to clear isol experiment api align with otel wide push for opt in experiment featur 2 http default client deprec otel http work deprec default http client usag is in progress post get helper reli on http defaultcli and limit configur follow up pr exist need review for inclus in upcom releas 3 observ work non block pr sever observ pr e g self observ for otel grpc are ongo not releas block\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"874202ba8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3581463689.md\", \"id\": \"48e05b84bee0afed\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.33800998676608723, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.17307692395155322, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7228538, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3581463689.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874202ba8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3581463689.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3581463689.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 3959, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:22\", \"token_count\": 1379, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"    - Problem statement\\n\\n    - Alternatives\\n\\n    - Pros/cons\\n\\n    - Links to Go runtime and `pprof` semantics\\n\\n  - Keep current large PR as draft / proof of concept.\\n\\n### 2. Reviews & Contributor Support\\n\\n- Maintainers emphasized the need for **more PR reviews** (reviews from non-approvers are valuable).\\n\\n- Nico asked for smaller starter tasks.\\n\\n  - Suggested areas:\\n\\n    - Flaky tests in `opentelemetry-go-contrib`\\n\\n    - Open issues in core and contrib repositories\\n\\n- Meeting notes and active PR references are pinned in the repository for visibility.\\n\\n- Guidance:\\n\\n  - Prefer **atomic PRs** (one change per PR).\\n\\n  - If a PR contains “and”, it likely should be split.\\n\\n  - Assigned issues may be stale — double-check activity before skipping.\\n\\n### 3. New Contributor Introduction\\n\\n- Michal introduced himself and offered help.\\n\\n- Requested onboarding guidance / buddy support.\\n\\n- Recommendations:\\n\\n  - Review `CONTRIBUTING.md`\\n\\n  - Browse open issues and PRs\\n\\n  - Ask on Slack for direction or clarification\\n\\n### 4. Kafka & Auto-Instrumentation Placement\\n\\n- Question: Why some auto-instrumentations (e.g., Kafka) live in `opentelemetry-go` instead of `contrib`?\\n\\n- Context:\\n\\n  - Some instrumentations were historical donations.\\n\\n  - Sarama instrumentation was deprecated and moved under Shopify due to lack of maintainers.\\n\\n  - Auto-instrumentation landscape in Go is fragmented:\\n\\n    - eBPF-based approaches\\n\\n    - Compile-time instrumentation\\n\\n    - Separate Auto-Instrumentation SIG\\n\\n- Recommendation:\\n\\n  - Join the Go Auto-Instrumentation SIG meeting.\\n\\n  - Use the dedicated Slack channel for deeper discussion.\\n\\n### 5. Community Announcements\\n\\n- Reminder: OpenTelemetry event (unconference style) in Brussels, Monday after FOSDEM (early February).\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-08]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2026-02-27\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3974113940  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2026-02-27T17:20:46Z · **Updated**: 2026-02-27T17:21:05Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"problem statement altern pro con link to go runtim and pprof semant keep current larg pr a draft proof of concept 2 review contributor support maintain emphas the need for more pr review review from non approv are valuabl nico ask for smaller starter task suggest area flaki test in opentelemetri go contrib open issu in core and contrib repositori meet note and activ pr refer are pin in the repositori for visibl guidanc prefer atom pr one chang per pr if a pr contain and it like should be split assign issu may be stale doubl check activ befor skip 3 new contributor introduct michal introduc himself and offer help request onboard guidanc buddi support recommend review contribut md brows open issu and pr ask on slack for direct or clarif 4 kafka auto instrument placement question whi some auto instrument e g kafka live in opentelemetri go instead of contrib context some instrument were histor donat sarama instrument wa deprec and move under shopifi due to lack of maintain auto instrument landscap in go is fragment ebpf base approach compil time instrument separ auto instrument sig recommend join the go auto instrument sig meet use the dedic slack channel for deeper discuss 5 communiti announc remind opentelemetri event unconfer style in brussel monday after fosdem earli februari sourc id src note 08 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2026 02 27 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3974113940 author pellar creat 2026 02 27t17 20 46z updat 2026 02 27t17 21 05z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8738b66a8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3974113940.md\", \"id\": \"4b8c459ac941782a\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.33418375831878694, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.15384615474112423, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7549715, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3974113940.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8738b66a8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3974113940.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3974113940.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 3929, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:30\", \"token_count\": 1330, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"  - Damien: Create a community issue to drive a cross-team ownership and operations proposal; invite GC (Governing Committee), comms/docs team, Collector maintainers, Go instrumentation, eBPF instrumentation, eBPF profiler, and this SIG.\\n\\n  - Damien: Propose strawman ownership models (Go SIG owning vs. comms/docs owning), required access (“keys”), and operational processes (DNS change notifications, rollout, playbooks).\\n\\n  - Tyler: Outline notification/subscription approach for DNS/CAA changes affecting serving; suggest checks-and-balances process.\\n\\n  - Group: Align on clear owner, permissions, and ops plan before any platform migration decision.\\n\\n### 2) PR: Add internal observability to OTLP Trace gRPC package; instrumentation scope naming\\n\\n- Summary:\\n\\n  - PR introduces internal observability instrumentation to the OTLP Trace gRPC package.\\n\\n  - Debate on scope name: use the instrumentation library/package path (current proposal) vs. the instrumented package/component name.\\n\\n- Discussion highlights:\\n\\n  - Specification guidance: instrumentation scope name should reflect the instrumentation library (not the instrumented target). Current proposal aligns with spec.\\n\\n  - Concern about stability: using internal package paths can constrain future internal code reorganization if dashboards/processors depend on the scope name.\\n\\n  - Proposal to add an attribute indicating the “instrumented component/package” to aid filtering/search, while keeping the scope name aligned with spec.\\n\\n- Decisions:\\n\\n  - Proceed with scope name per spec (instrumentation library).\\n\\n  - Consider adding an attribute to identify the instrumented component in a follow-up, potentially informed by spec work.\\n\\n- Action items:\\n\\n  - Tyler: Resolve the review thread referencing spec guidance; request/collect approvals.\\n\\n  - Robert: Open/track a semantic conventions issue to define an attribute for “instrumented component” across instrumentation.\\n\\n  - Group: Review PR; provide approvals.\\n\\n### 3) PR: Error type improvements (semantic conventions alignment)\\n\\n- Summary:\\n\\n  - Improve error typing so the error.type attribute reflects domain-specific values (e.g., gRPC status, partial error details) rather than generic “error string.”\\n\\n- Discussion highlights:\\n\\n  - Parser update allows passing errors that return a domain-relevant “type” string for telemetry.\\n\\n  - Fallback remains to package/type name if no domain-specific type is available.\\n\\n- Decisions:\\n\\n  - General agreement on direction; proceed after minor doc checks.\\n\\n- Action items:\\n\\n  - Robert: Verify GoDoc/rendering for the error type interface/docs (e.g., lines noted in error_type.go); approve once confirmed.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"damien creat a communiti issu to drive a cross team ownership and oper propos invit gc govern committe comm doc team collector maintain go instrument ebpf instrument ebpf profil and this sig damien propos strawman ownership model go sig own v comm doc own requir access key and oper process dns chang notif rollout playbook tyler outlin notif subscript approach for dns caa chang affect serv suggest check and balanc process group align on clear owner permiss and op plan befor ani platform migrat decis 2 pr add intern observ to otlp trace grpc packag instrument scope name summari pr introduc intern observ instrument to the otlp trace grpc packag debat on scope name use the instrument librari packag path current propos v the instrument packag compon name discuss highlight specif guidanc instrument scope name should reflect the instrument librari not the instrument target current propos align with spec concern about stabil use intern packag path can constrain futur intern code reorgan if dashboard processor depend on the scope name propos to add an attribut indic the instrument compon packag to aid filter search while keep the scope name align with spec decis proceed with scope name per spec instrument librari consid ad an attribut to identifi the instrument compon in a follow up potenti inform by spec work action item tyler resolv the review thread referenc spec guidanc request collect approv robert open track a semant convent issu to defin an attribut for instrument compon across instrument group review pr provid approv 3 pr error type improv semant convent align summari improv error type so the error type attribut reflect domain specif valu e g grpc status partial error detail rather than generic error string discuss highlight parser updat allow pass error that return a domain relev type string for telemetri fallback remain to packag type name if no domain specif type is avail decis general agreement on direct proceed after minor doc check action item robert verifi godoc render for the error type interfac doc e g line note in error _ type go approv onc confirm\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"873c8ee88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3389972183.md\", \"id\": \"2c0f90309d6fb812\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.33104143831878696, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.15384615474112423, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7444971, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3389972183.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"873c8ee88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3389972183.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3389972183.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 8301, \"chunk_count\": 7, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:30\", \"token_count\": 3187, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-06]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-03\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3479655348  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-03T09:39:04Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-03T09:40:01Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-10-30\\n\\n**Attendees:**\\n\\n- Tyler Yahn\\n\\n- Bryan Boreham\\n\\n- Damien Mathieu\\n\\n- Robert Pająk\\n\\n- David Ashpole\\n\\n- Mike Blum\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n### Monitoring bugs reported by OSS-Fuzz\\n\\n- David proposed enabling automatic filing of OSS-Fuzz findings as GitHub issues to track and triage them in-repo.\\n\\n- Robert noted OSS-Fuzz runs in Google CI; access and notifications currently limited. Some maintainers may need to be added as contacts.\\n\\n- Tyler and David highlighted that OSS-Fuzz does not file public issues by default due to potential security sensitivity of fuzz findings.\\n\\n- Consensus:\\n\\n  - Start by setting up a maintainers mailing list for OSS-Fuzz notifications (via GC) and trial monitoring for a few months.\\n\\n  - Avoid enabling public GitHub issue filing for now; reassess after triage/verification workflows are in place.\\n\\n  - Robert can manually recreate older issues if needed.\\n\\n- Bryan shared Prometheus project’s recent discussion comparing OSS-Fuzz with Go’s built-in fuzzing; Robert emphasized OSS-Fuzz’s continuous background fuzzing as a benefit.\\n\\nReferences:\\n\\n- [Monitoring bugs reported by OSS Fuzz #7549](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/7549)\\n\\n### Stabilization of otelgrpc\\n\\n- Community request to stabilize otelgrpc noted by Tyler.\\n\\n- Blockers:\\n\\n  - Stabilization of RPC semantic conventions (semconv) must come first.\\n\\n  - Audit of the current otelgrpc API to remove cruft and confirm stability.\\n\\n- Damien clarified that stabilization does not imply restoring the old interceptor—it should remain removed.\\n\\n- David is willing to drive module stability once semconv stabilizes; however, gRPC engagement has been sporadic and driven by their internal roadmap.\\n\\n- Strategy discussion:\\n\\n  - OTel could continue owning and maintaining a gRPC instrumentation package, with the option to deprecate later if gRPC ships native instrumentation aligned with semconv.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src note 06 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 03 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3479655348 author pellar creat 2025 11 03t09 39 04z updat 2025 11 03t09 40 01z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 10 30 attende tyler yahn bryan boreham damien mathieu robert paj ą k david ashpol mike blum transcript monitor bug report by os fuzz david propos enabl automat file of os fuzz find a github issu to track and triag them in repo robert note os fuzz run in googl ci access and notif current limit some maintain may need to be ad a contact tyler and david highlight that os fuzz doe not file public issu by default due to potenti secur sensit of fuzz find consensus start by set up a maintain mail list for os fuzz notif via gc and trial monitor for a few month avoid enabl public github issu file for now reassess after triag verif workflow are in place robert can manual recreat older issu if need bryan share prometheus project s recent discuss compar os fuzz with go s built in fuzz robert emphas os fuzz s continu background fuzz a a benefit refer monitor bug report by os fuzz 7549 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 7549 stabil of otelgrpc communiti request to stabil otelgrpc note by tyler blocker stabil of rpc semant convent semconv must come first audit of the current otelgrpc api to remov cruft and confirm stabil damien clarifi that stabil doe not impli restor the old interceptor it should remain remov david is will to drive modul stabil onc semconv stabil howev grpc engag ha been sporad and driven by their intern roadmap strategi discuss otel could continu own and maintain a grpc instrument packag with the option to deprec later if grpc ship nativ instrument align with semconv\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"874039c68a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"id\": \"37d8c65557d9108d\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.32457547831878697, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.15384615474112423, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7229439, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874039c68a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 7597, \"chunk_count\": 4, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:24\", \"token_count\": 1926, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"\\treturn err\\n\\n}\\n\\nreturn nil\\n\\n```\\n\\nOr, should we record this error?\\n\\n```go\\n\\nctx, span := tracer.Tracer(instrumentationName).Start(ctx, \\\"example\\\")\\n\\ndefer span.End()\\n\\nerr := query(ctx, db)\\n\\nif err != nil {\\n\\n\\tspan.RecordError(err)\\n\\n\\treturn err\\n\\n}\\n\\nreturn nil\\n\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\nI don't think we should just ignore the error without recording it in the span. `RecordError` has `semconv.ExceptionMessage(err.Error())` to record error message, which is always useful when debugging.\\n\\nAre you trying to limit the usage of `RecordError` to only instrumentation? Why can the instrumentation record the error message?\\n\\n---\\n\\n**pellared** — 2025-08-04T15:12:11Z\\n\\n> For instance, when facing code like this,\\n\\nIt looks like a **terminating** error to me which falls into https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions/blob/main/docs/general/recording-errors.md#recording-errors-on-spans:\\n\\n> When the operation ends with an error, instrumentation:\\n\\n---\\n\\n**XSAM** — 2025-08-05T06:38:55Z\\n\\nI see. So, your proposal is\\n\\n```go\\n\\nctx, span := tracer.Tracer(instrumentationName).Start(ctx, \\\"example\\\")\\n\\ndefer span.End()\\n\\nerr := query(ctx, db)\\n\\nif err != nil {\\n\\n\\tspan.SetAttributes(semconv.ErrorType(err))\\n\\n\\tspan.SetStatus(codes.Error, err.Error())\\n\\n\\treturn err\\n\\n}\\n\\nreturn nil\\n\\n```\\n\\nIt makes sense.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**pellared** — 2025-08-05T06:40:03Z\\n\\nCorrect \\n\\n---\\n\\n**XSAM** — 2025-08-05T06:50:03Z\\n\\n> In such cases, recording retry attempts as span events via span.RecordError gives users better visibility into transient issues without prematurely ending the span.\\n\\nWould it be strange to say we only record `exception` events when `panic` and retriable error happens? Retriable errors do not seem to be categorized as a type of `exception`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**pellared** — 2025-11-03T13:34:57Z\\n\\nMy plan is to add OTel Go specfic \\\"recording errors\\\" guidelines into our [Style Guide](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#style-guide). Maybe it should be part of some more public user-facing docs like https://pkg.go.dev/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/trace. However, I prefer first trying it out more internally. One of the reasons is that https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions/blob/main/docs/general/recording-errors.md#recording-errors-on-spans is \\\"Development\\\" and would need to be \\\"Stable\\\" first. I would work on it on the scope of:\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"return err return nil or should we record this error go ctx span tracer tracer instrumentationnam start ctx exampl defer span end err queri ctx db if err nil span recorderror err return err return nil i don t think we should just ignor the error without record it in the span recorderror ha semconv exceptionmessag err error to record error messag which is alway use when debug are you tri to limit the usag of recorderror to onli instrument whi can the instrument record the error messag pellar 2025 08 04t15 12 11z for instanc when face code like this it look like a termin error to me which fall into http github com open telemetri semant convent blob main doc general record error md record error on span when the oper end with an error instrument xsam 2025 08 05t06 38 55z i see so your propos is go ctx span tracer tracer instrumentationnam start ctx exampl defer span end err queri ctx db if err nil span setattribut semconv errortyp err span setstatus code error err error return err return nil it make sens pellar 2025 08 05t06 40 03z correct xsam 2025 08 05t06 50 03z in such case record retri attempt a span event via span recorderror give user better visibl into transient issu without prematur end the span would it be strang to say we onli record except event when panic and retriabl error happen retriabl error do not seem to be categor a a type of except pellar 2025 11 03t13 34 57z my plan is to add otel go specfic record error guidelin into our style guid http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go blob main contribut md style guid mayb it should be part of some more public user face doc like http pkg go dev go opentelemetri io otel trace howev i prefer first tri it out more intern one of the reason is that http github com open telemetri semant convent blob main doc general record error md record error on span is develop and would need to be stabl first i would work on it on the scope of\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8745fc628a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"id\": \"062966a1a409f1ea\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3032666914241864, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11538461632026624, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7416582, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8745fc628a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 15479, \"chunk_count\": 9, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:22\", \"token_count\": 4323, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"*   David also mentioned ongoing work on exponential histograms and a simpler \\\"last value\\\" PR that shares code with the histogram one.\\n\\n*   Tyler expressed a strong desire to merge the histogram reservoir PR in the current milestone due to its significant performance improvement and encouraged attendees to review it.\\n\\n**6. Milestone Check-in and Release Goals**\\n\\n*   Tyler conducted a check-in on the v1.39.0 milestones for [Otel](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/milestone/74) and [Contrib](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/milestone/33).\\n\\n*   **Exposed Temporality Selector Function PR:** Tyler noted that a previous SIG meeting concluded this PR was API pollution and should be closed. He will draft a comment and close it today.\\n\\n*   **Simple Span Processor (Tracing):** This PR needs another round of reviews but is considered straightforward and should remain in the milestone.\\n\\n*   **OTLP Metric GRPC Exporter Metrics:** This PR has been open for a while and needs more iteration. It might be moved out of the current milestone if a release push occurs.\\n\\n*   **Metrics SDK Standard Out Metrics Exporter & Standard Log Exporter:** Both PRs lack follow-up from their original authors and significant work is still needed. They are candidates for being bumped from the milestone.\\n\\n*   **Overall Release Strategy:** Tyler proposed making a release before KubeCon (less than a month away) and urged everyone to prioritize reviews for the critical PRs to achieve this goal.\\n\\n**7. KubeCon Discussion**\\n\\n*   **David Ashpole** asked if there was anything specific to announce or discuss at KubeCon.\\n\\n*   **Robert Pająk** mentioned the extended attributes merge in specification and product as something he'd like to highlight, though it's not ready.\\n\\n*   **Tyler Yahn** expressed interest in showcasing the new observability features.\\n\\n*   David suggested working towards a stable release of the HTTP instrumentation in Contrib. Tyler agreed it was a good idea but noted the significant work involved due to existing \\\"cruft\\\" and potential needs for API restructuring.\\n\\n**8. Tyler's Side Project (OTLP Exporter Error Types)**\\n\\n*   Tyler shared that he's been working on introducing new, custom error types for OTLP exporters to provide clearer, more unified error messages. This involves distinguishing between HTTP/gRPC errors, partial errors, and warnings. He has a prototype integrated for Otel Trace gRPC. While not critical, it improves observability and user understanding of errors.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"david also mention ongo work on exponenti histogram and a simpler last valu pr that share code with the histogram one tyler express a strong desir to merg the histogram reservoir pr in the current mileston due to it signific perform improv and encourag attende to review it 6 mileston check in and releas goal tyler conduct a check in on the v1 39 0 mileston for otel http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go mileston 74 and contrib http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib mileston 33 expos tempor selector function pr tyler note that a previous sig meet conclud this pr wa api pollut and should be close he will draft a comment and close it today simpl span processor trace this pr need anoth round of review but is consid straightforward and should remain in the mileston otlp metric grpc export metric this pr ha been open for a while and need more iter it might be move out of the current mileston if a releas push occur metric sdk standard out metric export standard log export both pr lack follow up from their origin author and signific work is still need they are candid for be bump from the mileston overal releas strategi tyler propos make a releas befor kubecon less than a month away and urg everyon to priorit review for the critic pr to achiev this goal 7 kubecon discuss david ashpol ask if there wa anyth specif to announc or discus at kubecon robert paj ą k mention the extend attribut merg in specif and product a someth he d like to highlight though it s not readi tyler yahn express interest in showcas the new observ featur david suggest work toward a stabl releas of the http instrument in contrib tyler agre it wa a good idea but note the signific work involv due to exist cruft and potenti need for api restructur 8 tyler s side project otlp export error type tyler share that he s been work on introduc new custom error type for otlp export to provid clearer more unifi error messag this involv distinguish between http grpc error partial error and warn he ha a prototyp integr for otel trace grpc while not critic it improv observ and user understand of error\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"873e60b08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"id\": \"fc13fa8c97d8e3a2\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.30191873142418635, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11538461632026624, \"vector_similarity\": 0.737165, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"873e60b08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 8756, \"chunk_count\": 4, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:25\", \"token_count\": 2164, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"My proposal is to not use `span.RecordError` for **terminating errors** per [recording errors on spans semantic conventions](https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions/blob/main/docs/general/recording-errors.md#recording-errors-on-spans).\\n\\nDuring the SIG meeting, it was also noted that `span.RecordError` captures a stack trace. However, since the stack trace reflects where the error was recorded, not where it originated, I don’t find it particularly valuable. Additionally, capturing and emitting a stack trace has a performance cost. In most languages with exception handling (such as Java or .NET), the stack trace is already included in the thrown exception so the cost of capturing the stack trace was already taken and the stack trace is taken in the place where the exception was thrown.\\n\\n> @pellared does that mean span.RecordError should essentially never be called by instrumentation, since panic recovery is already handled by the SDK? Almost makes it seem like we should deprecate RecordError in the API,\\n\\nI believe [`span.RecordError`](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-specification/blob/main/specification/trace/api.md#record-exception) remains valuable, particularly for **non-terminating errors**. A common use case is **retry logic**, where errors occur but don't immediately end the span. This is especially relevant in the context of **custom instrumentation**, where developers have full control and can explicitly record such intermediate errors.\\n\\nWhile instrumentation libraries typically just return errors, they could also benefit from `span.RecordError` if the underlying library provides hooks into retry or failure logic. In such cases, recording retry attempts as span events via `span.RecordError` gives users better visibility into transient issues **without prematurely ending the span**.\\n\\nFor these reasons, I don’t think `span.RecordError` should be deprecated. It might be worth capturing these use cases in the [error recording semantic conventions](https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions/blob/main/docs/general/recording-errors.md) (cc @lmolkova).\\n\\nSide note: There is an OTEP https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-specification/pull/4333 that proposes to record exceptions/errors as log records instead of span events.\\n\\n>  and document that End should handle recording exceptions for panics.\\n\\nI think that documenting that `span.End` should handle recording exceptions for panics is a good idea.\\n\\nIn my opinion, this is how we implement [recording an exception](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-specification/blob/main/specification/trace/exceptions.md#recording-an-exception) in the most possible user-friendly way.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"my propos is to not use span recorderror for termin error per record error on span semant convent http github com open telemetri semant convent blob main doc general record error md record error on span dure the sig meet it wa also note that span recorderror captur a stack trace howev sinc the stack trace reflect where the error wa record not where it origin i don t find it particular valuabl addit captur and emit a stack trace ha a perform cost in most languag with except handl such a java or net the stack trace is alreadi includ in the thrown except so the cost of captur the stack trace wa alreadi taken and the stack trace is taken in the place where the except wa thrown pellar doe that mean span recorderror should essenti never be call by instrument sinc panic recoveri is alreadi handl by the sdk almost make it seem like we should deprec recorderror in the api i believ span recorderror http github com open telemetri opentelemetri specif blob main specif trace api md record except remain valuabl particular for non termin error a common use case is retri logic where error occur but don t immedi end the span this is especi relev in the context of custom instrument where develop have full control and can explicit record such intermedi error while instrument librari typic just return error they could also benefit from span recorderror if the under librari provid hook into retri or failur logic in such case record retri attempt a span event via span recorderror give user better visibl into transient issu without prematur end the span for these reason i don t think span recorderror should be deprec it might be worth captur these use case in the error record semant convent http github com open telemetri semant convent blob main doc general record error md cc lmolkova side note there is an otep http github com open telemetri opentelemetri specif pull 4333 that propos to record except error a log record instead of span event and document that end should handl record except for panic i think that document that span end should handl record except for panic is a good idea in my opinion this is how we implement record an except http github com open telemetri opentelemetri specif blob main specif trace except md record an except in the most possibl user friend way\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8745fc628a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"id\": \"085f95b8d9b42db9\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.30161207142418633, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11538461632026624, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7361428, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8745fc628a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 15479, \"chunk_count\": 9, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:22\", \"token_count\": 4323, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}], \"pagination\": {\"page\": 1, \"page_size\": 10, \"total_chunks\": 70, \"total_pages\": 7}, \"query_info\": {\"question\": \"Go SIG Nico large runtime-tracer profiling public API proposal decision\", \"similarity_threshold\": 0.2, \"vector_weight\": 0.3, \"keyword_search\": false, \"dataset_count\": 1}}"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"agent_message","text":"The Go SIG decided **not to merge the large public-API proposal as submitted**. They wanted an incremental path instead:\n\n- Keep the current PR as a draft/proof of concept.\n- First add a small, focused change—such as allowing runtime-tracer integration to be disabled.\n- Have Nico open an issue documenting the profiling problem, alternatives, semantics, and trade-offs before further API work.\n\n[Source record: SRC-NOTE-08](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3974113940)"}}
